{"repositoryId":1290248611,"availability":"available","full":"brittanysmart/earned-autonomy","name":"earned-autonomy","description":"A human-in-the-loop approval layer for AI agents: an agent proposes actions with a confidence score, and a human approves, edits, or rejects each before it runs. Autonomy is earned per-action, not granted by default. The app is Plumb, demoed on a documentation agent.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-05T18:39:32Z","updated":"2026-07-29T22:53:02Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://plumb-approval-queue.vercel.app","topics":["agent-governance","ai-agents","design-systems","human-in-the-loop","llm","nextjs"],"demo":"https://plumb-approval-queue.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T23:48:20.074Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T23:48:20.074Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T23:48:20.074Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T23:48:20.074Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An agent proposes. A person decides. Nothing runs until they do.","Under 90 confidence, a human decides. High risk, a human decides.","Those three rules are the product. The case study explains why."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brittanysmart/earned-autonomy/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d3d3ca573bd5b3aeba9386b140c9a9b102688e7d43e075bae5be8a909d42c43a","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T23:48:20.161Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T23:48:20.161Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An agent proposes. A person decides. Nothing runs until they do.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brittanysmart/earned-autonomy/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"d3d3ca573bd5b3aeba9386b140c9a9b102688e7d43e075bae5be8a909d42c43a","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brittanysmart/earned-autonomy/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-16T23:48:20.161Z"},"overviewRepoUpdate